password-blocklist.txt
======================

Common passwords rejected at registration (ADR 0002 §5.3, D5; NIST SP 800-63B §5.1.1.2).
Server-only: loaded from Nitro server assets, never shipped in the client bundle.

Source
------
SecLists, https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists
Commit dbdbd9ae1135fc53ecb0a9880af94178d0fc6264

  Passwords/Common-Credentials/xato-net-10-million-passwords-1000000.txt
    SHA-256 424a3e03a17df0a2bc2b3ca749d81b04e79d59cb7aeec8876a5a3f308d0caf51
    (Mark Burnett's 2015 "10 million passwords" dataset, top 1,000,000)
  Passwords/Common-Credentials/100k-most-used-passwords-NCSC.txt
    SHA-256 c2e5696882c603b76bb67a47ee970897e5a76fc4c3f5547abe3d0ca340c576e0
    (UK National Cyber Security Centre, derived from Have I Been Pwned)

Processing
----------
Each line is NFKC-normalized and lowercased. Lines with control characters are dropped. Only
entries of 12 to 128 Unicode code points are kept (the password length policy). The result is
de-duplicated and sorted (JavaScript default string order), one entry per line.
Result: 46,825 entries, SHA-256 79ae4140984c64d2a8cdb7dd07f27bc680ba5adf956c346bde96b32ec25faaec

Regenerate
----------
  pnpm auth:blocklist                # downloads the pinned files and verifies their SHA-256
  pnpm auth:blocklist --from <dir>   # uses local copies of the two files
Script: scripts/build-password-blocklist.ts

